Verification Test Plan for Unstable Bluff Detection System

Test Set 1: Risk Assessment (0-5)

Purpose: To verify that the system correctly identifies the risk level of bluff changes from 0 to 5 and sends an alert when necessary. 
Test approach: Our test approach will be partition-based.

Unit Testing: To determine whether the risk assessment component appropriately addresses each risk category, test it separately 
Risk 0 = indicates no identifiable change
Risk 1-3 = indicates signicant slide
Risk 4 = indicates significant change; immediate evaluation may be required.
Risk 5 = indicates major changes; immediate stop and evacuation required.

Integration Testing: Verify that Risk assessment and the alert system are interacting correctly. 
Risk 0-3 = no alert sent
Risk 4-5 = Alert sent to rail operators and lifeguards for immediate evaluation. 

System Testing: Test every aspect of the system, from the cameras taking pictures to the algorithm identifying danger and issuing a warning.
Input: Images representing a level from 0- 3 changes.
Output: The system determines the level and whether to send an alert or not
Input: Images representing a level from 4-5 changes
Output: The system determines that it needs to send an emergency alert.  

________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

Pseudocode for Test Set 1

TEST_SET system_end_to_end

    TEST low_change_images
        input = images representing a level from 0-3 changes
        run entire system (camera -> algorithm -> alert logic)
        ASSERT system determines the correct level
        ASSERT system decides whether to send an alert or not
              // expected: no alert

    TEST high_change_images
        input = images representing a level from 4-5 changes
        run entire system (camera -> algorithm -> alert logic)
        ASSERT system determines it needs to send an emergency alert



TEST_SET integration_risk_and_alert

    TEST no_alert_for_risk_0_to_3
        FOR level IN {0, 1, 2, 3}
            riskAssessment.setLevel(level)
            alertSystem.process(level)
            ASSERT alertSent == false

    TEST alert_for_risk_4_to_5
        FOR level IN {4, 5}
            riskAssessment.setLevel(level)
            alertSystem.process(level)
            ASSERT alertSent == true
            ASSERT recipients CONTAINS railOperators
            ASSERT recipients CONTAINS lifeguards




TEST_SET unit_risk_assessment          // partition-based

    TEST risk_0_no_change
        input  = image set showing no identifiable change
        ASSERT assessRisk(input) == 0

    TEST risk_1_to_3_significant_slide
        FOR EACH input IN image sets representing minor to significant slide
            ASSERT assessRisk(input) IN {1, 2, 3}

    TEST risk_4_significant_change
        input  = image set showing significant change
        ASSERT assessRisk(input) == 4        // immediate evaluation may be required

    TEST risk_5_major_change
        input  = image set showing major changes
        ASSERT assessRisk(input) == 5        // immediate stop and evacuation required

